1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,365
The top line or the bottom line —
which one is longer?

2
00:00:03,415 --> 00:00:09,135
Look only at the middle lines.
Top or bottom — which is longer?

3
00:00:09,185 --> 00:00:11,505
The bottom one looks longer, right?

4
00:00:11,555 --> 00:00:13,875
Let's draw lines straight down
from the ends of the top line

5
00:00:13,925 --> 00:00:16,045
Huh? They hit the ends
of the bottom line exactly!

6
00:00:16,095 --> 00:00:18,115
Let's measure them with a ruler

7
00:00:18,165 --> 00:00:20,485
Both are exactly 10 marks long!

8
00:00:20,535 --> 00:00:22,585
Take off the arrow ends…

9
00:00:22,635 --> 00:00:25,555
…and they're just two lines of the same length

10
00:00:25,605 --> 00:00:28,525
Put them back on…
even now that you know, the bottom still looks longer!

11
00:00:28,575 --> 00:00:30,695
Your brain doesn't measure
the middle line on its own

12
00:00:30,745 --> 00:00:33,465
It takes in the shapes on the ends too,
and guesses the length from the whole thing

13
00:00:33,515 --> 00:00:36,235
Ends that spread out make the whole thing bigger,
so the line feels longer

14
00:00:36,285 --> 00:00:40,205
Exactly why this happens
is something scientists are still studying

15
00:00:40,255 --> 00:00:44,375
Draw it on paper
and try it on a friend

16
00:00:44,425 --> 00:00:46,825
The same length can look different
depending on the ends

17
00:00:46,875 --> 00:00:49,325
NEXT: Two circles in the middle — which one is bigger?
